#: Community.md:1
msgid "Community and hierarchy"
msgstr "Community と階層"

#: Community.md:3
msgid ""
"When a developer writes a new PLUMED action, they are forced to decide where"
" the documentation for that action should appear in the manual. Should their"
" new PLMD::Action be listed as a collective variable, function, bias, or "
"something else?"
msgstr "開発者は新 PLMD::Action を CV、Function、Bias などマニュアルのどこに置くか決めます。"

#: Community.md:6
msgid ""
"I increasingly feel that these somewhat arbitrary and abstract "
"categorisations are not that useful. They force developers to think in terms"
" of a particular application domain. As the code grows, this limitation "
"makes less and less sense."
msgstr "この便宜的で抽象的な分類は有用性が薄いと感じます。特定の応用分野を強制し、拡大するコードにはますます合いません。"

#: Community.md:9
msgid ""
"Providing tools to document what can be done with the tools they implemented"
" in PLUMED is more beneficial. They can do this by submitting tutorials and,"
" if they so wish, they can even come up with their own categorisations for "
"the PLMD::Action objects in the code."
msgstr "何ができるかを文書化するツールの方が有益です。Tutorial を投稿し、必要なら独自の PLMD::Action 分類も使えます。"

#: Community.md:13
msgid ""
"In other words, different developers working in different application "
"domains should have the flexibility to document and categorise actions in a "
"way that makes sense for the particular application domain they are working "
"within. PLUMED is a community-developed code. If different people in the "
"community think differently about the code's functionalities, then the "
"documentation should be flexible enough to incorporate these different "
"views."
msgstr ""
"異なる分野の開発者が、分野に適した分類・説明をできる柔軟性が必要です。Community で開発するコードなので、多様な見方を文書に反映すべきです。"

#: Community.md:17
msgid ""
"Rather than thinking the code must have one manual, we should move to a "
"model of having many manuals. These manuals can then explain how the code is"
" used in practice."
msgstr "単一マニュアルではなく、実際の使い方を説明する複数マニュアルのモデルに移るべきです。"
